<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">

  <!--
    daemon-eliza.mml

    ELIZA-µ contract:
      Reasoning operator daemon — dispatches the 16 Pop+Sek operator pairs
      (CAUSE/CONTRAST/ANALOGY/DEDUCTION/INDUCTION/ABDUCTION/SYNTHESIS/
       DECOMPOSITION/REFRAME/CHALLENGE/SUPPORT/REDIRECT/QUESTION/COMPARE/PLAN/DIRECT)
      and runs Rogerian reflection patterns for intent elicitation.

      ELIZA spans two phases:
        Pop — introduces/seeds the reasoning frame for the incoming query
        Sek — executes the selected operator
      Primary registry phase is Pop; operator authority phase per operator varies.

    Implementation: src/micronaut/eliza_operators.cpp + src/micronaut/aiml_engine.cpp
    AIML corpus: data/alice/eliza.aiml, chat.aiml, greetings.aiml, inquiry.aiml,
                 interjection.aiml, salutations.aiml, continuation.aiml, that.aiml

    Content dictionary: urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1
  -->

  <!-- ── Identity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>eliza</mi><mo>_</mo><mi>&#x03BC;</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo>
      <mi>phase</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>role</mi>
      <mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <eq/>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">Identity</csymbol><ci>eliza</ci></apply>
        <list>
          <cn>Pop</cn>
          <cn>0.35</cn>
          <ci>ReasoningOperatorDaemon</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
eliza_mu = &lt;phase=Pop, T=0.35, role=ReasoningOperatorDaemon&gt;
Primary phase: Pop (seed/introduction) — introduces reasoning frame for query.
Secondary execution phase: Sek — Pop+Sek operator pair.
Temperature 0.35: low — ELIZA is pattern-based and near-deterministic.
Phase angle (Pop): theta = 0.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Capability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Cap</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>eliza</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>{</mo>
      <mi>OPERATOR_DISPATCH</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>ROGERIAN_REFLECT</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>INTENT_ELICIT</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>COMPARE</mi>
      <mo>}</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">Capability</csymbol>
        <ci>eliza</ci>
        <list>
          <ci>OPERATOR_DISPATCH</ci>
          <ci>ROGERIAN_REFLECT</ci>
          <ci>INTENT_ELICIT</ci>
          <ci>COMPARE</ci>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
CAN:
  OPERATOR_DISPATCH — routes to one of 16 reasoning operators:
    CAUSE, CONTRAST, ANALOGY, DEDUCTION, INDUCTION, ABDUCTION,
    SYNTHESIS, DECOMPOSITION, REFRAME, CHALLENGE, SUPPORT,
    REDIRECT, QUESTION, COMPARE, PLAN, DIRECT.
    Each is a Pop+Sek pair: Pop introduces the frame, Sek executes it.
  ROGERIAN_REFLECT — rephrases/reflects user input back ("Tell me more
    about X", "Why do you feel X?", "What makes you think X?") using
    AIML pattern matching in data/alice/{chat,greetings,inquiry,
    interjection,salutations,continuation,that}.aiml.
  INTENT_ELICIT — scaffolds query understanding by probing the user's
    intent before routing to an executor; surfaces ambiguity for the
    Omega gate.
  COMPARE — structured comparison operator; also dispatches via SRAI
    surface (XCFE COMPARE → executor=eliza, phase=Ch'en).

SUPPLIES: reasoning_frame (Pop output), operator_result (Sek output),
          reflection_response, intent_candidate, comparison_report.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Operator set ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Ops</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>eliza</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <msup><mi>O</mi><mn>16</mn></msup>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <mspace width="0.5em"/>
      <mi>&#x2200;</mi><mi>op</mi><mo>&#x2208;</mo><mi>Ops</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>op</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>Pop</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Sek</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">OperatorSet</csymbol>
        <cn>16</cn>
        <list>
          <ci>CAUSE</ci><ci>CONTRAST</ci><ci>ANALOGY</ci><ci>DEDUCTION</ci>
          <ci>INDUCTION</ci><ci>ABDUCTION</ci><ci>SYNTHESIS</ci><ci>DECOMPOSITION</ci>
          <ci>REFRAME</ci><ci>CHALLENGE</ci><ci>SUPPORT</ci><ci>REDIRECT</ci>
          <ci>QUESTION</ci><ci>COMPARE</ci><ci>PLAN</ci><ci>DIRECT</ci>
        </list>
        <list><ci>Pop</ci><ci>Sek</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
16 operators, each a Pop+Sek phase pair.
Pop (theta=0): introduces the reasoning frame — pattern-matches the query shape
  and selects which operator applies.
Sek (theta=pi): executes the operator — applies the selected reasoning transform.
Implementation: src/micronaut/eliza_operators.cpp.
ELIZA does not select the operator autonomously; XCFE routes the matched
frame to the appropriate operator based on the query structure.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── Authority boundary ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>&#x0394;B</mi><mo>&#x2209;</mo><mi>Auth</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>eliza</mi><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">AuthorityBoundary</csymbol>
        <apply><notin/><ci>DeltaTopology</ci><ci>Auth_eliza</ci></apply>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
CANNOT: commit topology, claim Ch'en verdict, mutate GramStore directly,
        or route to Xul unilaterally.
BOUNDARY: ELIZA produces reasoning_frame (Pop) and operator_result (Sek)
  as evidence. Ch'en verifies; XCFE authorizes; Xul commits.
  ELIZA's ROGERIAN_REFLECT output is evidence, not a fact commit.
  COMPARE output feeds evidence_refs for XCFE VERIFY, not the verdict itself.
Delta_B not-in Auth(eliza): topology commits require Proposal -> Ch'en -> XCFE -> Xul.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <!-- ── WCR scoring position ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <msub><mi>W</mi><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></msub>
      <mo>&#x22C5;</mo>
      <msub><mi>C</mi><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></msub>
      <mo>&#x22C5;</mo>
      <msub><mi>R</mi><mi>&#x03BC;</mi></msub>
      <mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <eq/>
        <ci>S</ci>
        <apply>
          <times/>
          <apply><selector/><ci>W</ci><ci>mu</ci></apply>
          <apply><selector/><ci>C</ci><ci>mu</ci></apply>
          <apply>
            <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">Relevance</csymbol>
            <ci>Q</ci>
          </apply>
        </apply>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
S = W_mu * C_mu * R_mu(Q)
W_mu: static weight; elevated for queries matching reflection/reasoning patterns.
C_mu: confidence from Ch'en-verified reasoning outcomes.
R_mu(Q): relevance peaks when Q contains reasoning operator triggers
  (CAUSE/CONTRAST/WHY/COMPARE/PLAN/etc.) or open-ended intent elicitation cues.
Eligibility: ELIZA admitted when requires(op) ⊆ {OPERATOR_DISPATCH, ROGERIAN_REFLECT,
  INTENT_ELICIT, COMPARE}. Not admitted for pure topic-lookup queries (→ ALICE-µ).
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <!-- ── Map / Filter / Fold at Pop+Sek ───────────────────────────────────── -->

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Map</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>[</mo>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>op</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>frame</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>]</mo><msub><mrow/><mi>i</mi></msub>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">map</csymbol>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">OpFrameSelect</csymbol></apply>
        <ci>Q</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Phase: Pop.
Map(f_op, Q) = [(op_i, frame_i)] for each of the 16 operators in Ops(eliza).
f_op matches Q against the operator's AIML trigger pattern;
frame_i is the reasoning frame yielded when the trigger fires.
Output type: list of (operator_id, reasoning_frame) pairs.
Pure transform — does not execute operators; builds the candidate surface.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Filter</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>trigger</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>candidates</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>[</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>|</mo>
      <mi>c</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>trigger&#x5F;score</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn>
      <mo>&#x2227;</mo>
      <mi>XCFE</mi><mo>&#x5F;</mo><mi>admits</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>op</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>]</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">filter</csymbol>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">TriggerAdmission</csymbol></apply>
        <ci>candidates</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Phase: Pop (eligibility) + Wo (XCFE admission gate).
Predicate P_trigger retains a candidate iff:
  (a) trigger_score > 0 — the operator's pattern fired on Q, and
  (b) XCFE_admits(c.op) — the operator is eligible under the current
      phase context (requires(op) ⊆ capabilities(eliza)).
Filter cannot substitute for XCFE admission; it consumes the admission result.
Rogerian reflection candidates pass when Q is open-ended or emotionally framed.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Fold</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>&#x2295;</mi><mi>primary</mi></msub><mo>,</mo>
      <mo>&#x22A5;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>filtered</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>=</mo><mi>reasoning&#x5F;frame</mi>
      <mspace width="0.5em"/>
      <mover><mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>Sek</mi></mover>
      <mspace width="0.5em"/>
      <mi>operator&#x5F;result</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:functional:v1">fold</csymbol>
        <apply><csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">PrimaryFrameSelect</csymbol></apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:daemon-eliza:v1">EmptyFrame</csymbol>
        <ci>filtered</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Phase: Pop → Sek.
Fold(⊕_primary, ⊥, filtered) reduces filtered candidates to the primary
reasoning_frame — the highest-scoring (op, frame) pair after W·C·R ranking.
The accumulated reasoning_frame is then passed to Sek for operator execution:
  Sek dispatches eliza_operators.cpp with the selected op and frame as inputs,
  producing operator_result.
Associativity not assumed; step ⊕_primary is W·C·R max-select, not sum.
Empty-input result is ⊥ (no frame selected) → Rogerian fallback reflection.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>SharedPatternKernelRef</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mtext>data/grammar/mml/v1/PatternKernelCalls.mml</mtext>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:pattern-kernel-calls:v1">UsesSharedPatternKernel</csymbol>
        <list><ci>MicronautPatterns</ci><ci>DaemonPatterns</ci><ci>SraiOperators</ci>
          <ci>aiml-functions</ci><ci>map-filter-fold</ci><ci>CheeseCritic</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Uses shared typed pattern-call contract. Invokes only registered operations
applicable to its role (Pop+Sek operator dispatch, Rogerian reflection).
The shared reference does not grant capabilities or execution authority.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
daemon-eliza contract invariants:
1. ELIZA is the reasoning operator daemon; it is not a general-purpose conversational daemon.
2. Every operator is a Pop+Sek pair; Pop introduces the frame, Sek executes it.
3. ROGERIAN_REFLECT output is evidence (intent_candidate); it is not a verified answer.
4. COMPARE output feeds evidence_refs; XCFE VERIFY issues the verdict.
5. ELIZA is not admitted for pure topic-lookup queries (those route to ALICE-µ).
6. Temperature 0.35 reflects the near-deterministic pattern-matching nature of ELIZA.
7. Topology commits require the full Proposal -> Ch'en -> XCFE -> Xul path.
  </annotation>
</math>
